  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:erc-1155",
  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "ERC-1155 is an Ethereum multi-token standard that allows a single smart contract to manage an arbitrary number of distinct token types \u2014 fungible, non-fungible, and semi-fungible \u2014 each identified by a uint256 token ID, with quantities tracked per address per ID. Pioneered by Enjin and formalised as EIP-1155, the standard introduces safeBatchTransferFrom for atomic multi-token transfers in a single transaction, substantially reducing gas costs compared to managing multiple separate ERC-20 or ERC-721 contracts. It is widely adopted in blockchain gaming, NFT collections, and on-chain economies that blend consumable items with unique assets.",
